2 CONT
2 CONT Philip II, Duke of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Bourbon (1438-1483) and had 3 children from this marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Louise (1476-1531), married Charles of Valois-Orléans, Count of Angoulême, had children including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis I of France whose daughter Margaret of Valois married to Emanuele Filiberto of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of Navarre (1492-1549); Queen consort of King Henry II of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Girolamo (1478)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Philibert II (Filiberto II) (1480-1504)
2 CONT
2 CONT Claudine or Claudina de Brosse of Brittany (1450-1513) and had 6 children from this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlo III (1486-1553) who succeeded his half-brother as Duke of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (1488-1502)
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip (1490-1533), duke of Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT Assolone (1494)
2 CONT
2 CONT Giovanni Amedeo (1495)
2 CONT
2 CONT Philiberta (1498-1524), married Julian II di Medici (1479-1516), duke of Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT He had also other 8 illegitimate children by 2 mistresses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Libera Portoneri
2 CONT
2 CONT René of Savoy (1468-31 March 1525) - served as Governor of Nice and Provence, known as the Grand Bastard of Savoy and father-in-law of Anne, 1st Duc de Montmorency.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonia of Savoy - married Jean II, Lord of Monaco
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter of Savoy - Bishop of Geneva
2 CONT
2 CONT Bona di Romagnano.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claudina (Claudia) of Savoy (d. 2 May 1528) - married to Jacob III, Count of Hornes (d. 15 August 1531).
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippina (Philippa) of Savoy - married Lorenzo de' Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT Margherita (Margaret) of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Giovanna (Johanna) of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Michele (Michael) of Savoy - a priest
