1 OCCU Abbot in San Giusto di Susa and in San Pietro di Rivalta (1498-1510), Ct of Geneva, Barone di Faucigny (1514-33), Marchese di Saint-Sorlin, Barone di Beaufort, Duc de Nemours (1516-33), Bp of Geneva, Filippo
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_de_Savoie,_1st_Duc_de_Nemours '''Philippe de Savoie''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe, Duke of Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Philippe de Savoie, 1st Duc de Nemours)
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of Arms of the Dukes of Savoy after Emmanuel Philibert
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe de Savoie, duc de Nemours (1490 – November 25, 1533) was a son of Philip II, Duke of Savoy, and brother of Louise of Savoy, mother of Francis I of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Originally destined for the priesthood, he was given the bishopric of Geneva at the age of five, but resigned it in 1510, when he was made count of Genevois. He served under Louis XII, with whom he was present at the battle of Agn
2 CONC adello (1509), under the emperor Charles V in 1520, and finally under his nephew, Francis I. In 1528 Francis gave him the duchy of Nemours and married him to Charlotte of Orleans-Longueville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise de Savoie 	Duke of Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT 1528–1533 	Succeeded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques de Savoie
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * This article incorporates text from the Encyclopædia Britannica, Eleventh Edition, a publication now in the public domain.
2 CONT
