1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alfonso IV d'Este, Duca di Modena (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #101400, b. 13 February 1634, d. 16 July 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=30 Sep 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.7%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Alfonso IV d'Este, Duca di Modena was born on 13 February 1634. He is the son of Francesco I d'Este, Duca di Modena and Mary Farnese. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Laura Martinozzi, daughter of Hieronymus Martinozzi and Laura Mazarini, on 27 May 1655. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 16 July 1662 at age 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Alfonso IV d'Este, Duca di Modena succeeded to the title of Duca di Modena in 1658. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alfonso IV d'Este, Duca di Modena and Laura Martinozzi
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Mary Beatrice Eleanora Anne Margaret Isabella d'Este+ b. 5 Oct 1658, d. 7 May 1718 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alfonso IV d'Este, Duca di Modena
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Francesco II d'Este, Duca di Modena b. 6 Mar 1660, d. 6 Sep 1694 (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10140.htm#i101400
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_IV_d%27Este,_Duke_of_Modena
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso IV d'Este (2 February 1634 – 16 July 1662) was Duke of Modena and Reggio from 1658 until his death. He was the father of Mary of Modena, consort of James II of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso was born in Modena, the eldest son of Francesco I d'Este, Duke of Modena, and his first wife, Maria Caterina Farnese. He became Duke of Modena and Reggio after his father's death in 1658. Alfonso's health was poor and he s
2 CONC uffered from gout and tuberculosis. He died four years into his reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1655 he married Laura Martinozzi, Cardinal Mazarin's niece, thus strengthening his alliance with France. On Laura's sixteenth birthday, 27 May 1655, she was married to the Duke of Modena by proxy at the Palace of Compiègne, wit
2 CONC h the Count of Soissons standing in the place of the Duke of Modena. They had two children, Maria and Francesco, who went on to become Queen of England and Duke of Modena respectively.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1659 the Franco-Spanish War came to an end and Modena was rewarded with the town of Correggio for supporting France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his two-year-old son, under the regency of his widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LT5N-XDM
