2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the ninth of eleven children of Leopold, Duke of Lorraine, and Élisabeth Charlotte d'Orléans, niece of Louis XIV. Her eldest brother became Francis I, Holy Roman Emperor, four years after her death. Maria Theresa of Austri
2 CONC a was her sister in law; thus she was an aunt of Marie Antoinette and Maria Carolina of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father died in 1729 when she was 17. She and her sister were proposed as wives for their first cousin, the widowed Louis d'Orléans, Duke of Orléans. He refused outright, much to the annoyance of her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was named the coadjutrice of Remiremont Abbey on 19 October 1734; Remiremont was closely associated with the Lorraine's. Her older sister Anne Charlotte was later the abbess of the prestigious institution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the marriage of her brother, the Lorraine family became a rather attactive family to marry into, two daughters of Charles VI, Holy Roman Emperor having done so already; the already twice widowed Charles Emmanuel III of Sardin
2 CONC ia asked for her hand in marriage and the marriage went ahead.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married the king of Sardinia by proxy on 5 March 1737 with the Prince of Carignan acting as the king, who was the prince's brother in law[1]. The couple married in person on 1 April 1737; Charles Emmanuel was her first cousin,
2 CONC  his mother being Anne Marie d'Orléans - older half sister of her mother Élisabeth Charlotte. The marriage produced three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth Theresa died at the Palace of Venaria at the age of 29, of complications of the birth of her last child. She was buried in the Cathedral S. Giovanni Battista, and moved in 1786 to the Basilica of Superga in Turin.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1775, her youngest son Benedetto married his niece but the couple had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Prince Carlo Francesco Maria Augusto of Savoy, Duke of Aosta (1 December 1738 – 25 March 1745)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Princess Vittoria Margherita of Savoy (Turin, 22 June 1740 - Turin, 14 July 1742)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Prince Benedetto Maria Maurizio of Savoy, Duke of Chablais, (Turin, 21 June 1741 - Turin, 4 January 1808)
2 CONT
2 CONT References and notes
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ The prince of Carignan had married Maria Vittoria Francesca of Savoy, illegitimate daughter of Charles Emmanuel's father Victor Amadeus II and Jeanne Baptiste d'Albert de Luynes
2 CONT
