1 NOTE "Bonnie Prince Charlie"
1 NOTE FULL NAME "CHARLES EDWARD LOUIS JOHN CASIMIR SILVESTER MARIA"; KNOWN AS "THE
2 CONT YOUNG PRETENDER""BONNIE PRINCE CHARLIE"; LATER THE JACOBITE CHARLES III
1 NOTE He was called The Young Pretender, The Young Chevalier, and Bonnie Prince 
2 CONT Charlie, claimant to the British throne who led the Scottish Highland army 
2 CONT in the Forty-five Rebellion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1744, after his father had obtained the support of the French 
2 CONT government for a projected invasion of England, Charles Edward went to 
2 CONT France to assume command of the French expeditionary forces. Unfavorable 
2 CONT weather and the mobilization of a powerful British fleet to oppose the 
2 CONT invasion led to cancellation of the plan by the French government. Charles 
2 CONT Edward persisted in his determination to drive George II from the British 
2 CONT throne, however, and in 1745 he arrived in Scotland, where a number of 
2 CONT Highland clans came to his assistance. He took Edinburgh, defeated a 
2 CONT British force at Prestonpans, and advanced as far south as Derby, England, 
2 CONT before being forced to retreat. In April 1746, however, his forces were 
2 CONT utterly routed at Culloden Moor. He was hunted as a fugitive for more than 
2 CONT five months, but the Highlanders never betrayed him, and he escaped to 
2 CONT France in September 1746. Two years later he was expelled from that 
2 CONT country in accordance with one of the provisions of the second Treaty of 
2 CONT Aix-la-Chapelle (1748), which stipulated that all members of the house of 
2 CONT Stuart were to be driven from France. For a number of years Charles Edward 
2 CONT wandered about Europe. Secretly visiting London in 1750 and in 1754, he 
2 CONT attempted without success on both occasions to win support for his cause. 
2 CONT In 1766, on his father's death, Charles Edward returned to Italy, where he 
2 CONT spent his last years.
