2 CONT
2 CONT Known before 1747 as Lady Emily Lennox, from 1747 to 1761 as The Countess of Kildare and from 1761 to 1766 as The Marchioness of Kildare. Despite her second marriage, she remained known as the Duchess of Leinster.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Charles Lennox, 2nd Duke of Richmond (who was illegitimately descended from King Charles II of England and one of his mistresses), and Sarah Lennox, Duchess of Richmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was presented at court at the age 13, and in 1745 aged 14, became engaged to James FitzGerald.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 James FitzGerald, 20th Earl of Kildare, on 7 Feb 1747, died 1773
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 William Ogilvie (her children's tutor, and with whom she had begun an affair some years earlier, and who was the natural father of her youngest son from her first marriage) on 26 Aug 1774
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT George FitzGerald, Earl of Offaly 1748 – 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT William FitzGerald 1749 – 1804
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Caroline FitzGerald 1750 – 1754
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Emily Mary FitzGerald 1751 – 1818
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Henrietta FitzGerald 1753 – 1763
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Caroline FitzGerald born and died April 1755
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles FitzGerald 1756 – 1810
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Charlotte Mary Gertrude FitzGerald 1758 – 1836
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Louisa Bridget FitzGerald 1760 – 1765 Lord Henry FitzGerald 1761 – 1829
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Sophia Sarah Mary FitzGerald 1762 – 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Edward FitzGerald 1763 – 1798
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Robert Stephen FitzGerald 1765 – 1833
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Gerald FitzGerald 1766 – 1789
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Augustus FitzGerald 1767 – 1771
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Fanny FitzGerald 1770 – 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Lucy Anne FitzGerald 1771 – 1851
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Louisa FitzGerald 1772 – 1776
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord George Simon FitzGerald 1773 – 1783
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia Margaret Ogilvie 1775 – 1824
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte Ogilvie born and died 1777
2 CONT
2 CONT Emily Charlotte "Mimi" Ogilvie 1778 – 1832
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of her 19 children with Kildare were born at their Dublin home, Leinster House. Her later years were spent in London and a summer home in Wimbledon. She died on 27 Mar 1814 at her home in Grosvenor Place, London, and was buri
2 CONC ed in the family vault at Chichester cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1999, Aristocrats, a six-part limited television series, was based on the lives of Emily Lennox and her sisters.
