2 CONT "General George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarle KG PC (London, 8 April 1724 – 13 October 1772), styled Viscount Bury until 1754, becoming 3rd Earl of Albermale, (title of 1697), in 1757 on the death of his father, the 2nd Earl was a
2 CONC  British soldier nobleman best known for his capture of Havana in 1762 during the Seven Years' War."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''General George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarle''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * He held the office of Lord of the Bedchamber to the Duke of Cumberland.
2 CONT * He fought in the Battle of Fontenoy in 1745.
2 CONT * He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Chichester between 1746 and 1754.
2 CONT * He fought in the Battle of Culloden on 16 April 1746, when he bore the dispatches announcing the victory to London.
2 CONT * He was commander of the 20th Foot on 1 November 1749.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Albemarle [E., 1697] on 22 December 1754.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of 3rd Baron Ashford, of Ashford, Kent [E., 1697] on 22 December 1754. He succeeded to the title of 3rd Viscount Bury, co. Lancaster [E., 1697] on 22 December 1754. 
2 CONT * He was Colonel of the King's Own Regiment between 1755 and 1772.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Major-General on 1 February 1756.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Lieutenant-General on 1 April 1759.
2 CONT * He held the office of Keeper and Governor of Jersey on 28 January 1761.
2 CONT * He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) on 28 January 1761.
2 CONT * He was Commander-in-Chief of the reduction of the Havannas in 1762.
2 CONT * He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) on 25 July 1771.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of General in May 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p1680.htm#i16794
2 CONT * https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/2H2M-TPM/gen.-sir-george-keppel-3rd-earl-of-abermarle-1724-1772
2 CONT * https://www.britishmuseum.org/collection/term/BIOG82884
2 CONT * https://www.ghgraham.org/georgekeppel1724.html
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49562707/george-keppel
2 CONT
2 CONT General George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albermarle was the son of William Anne van Keppel, 2nd Earl of Albemarle and Lady Anne Lennox.
2 CONT He was baptised on 4 May 1724 at St. Martin-in-the-Fields Church, Covent Garden, London, England.He married Anne Miller, daughter of Sir John Miller, 4th Bt. and Susan Combe, on 20 April 1770. He died aged 48.
2 CONT He was buried on 22 October 1772 at Quidenham, Norfolk, England.
