1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Stoke Park History===
2 CONT
2 CONT "An urn commemorating Juliana Penn. 
2 CONT On 30 June 1798 the painter Joseph Farington wrote in his diary:  ‘In 1702 father of the present Mr Penn was born, did not marry till he was 48 years of age, when he married Lady Juliana Fermor. Thus Mr Penn, is grandson to Willia
2 CONC m Penn, a remarkable circumstance; only 3 generations in 158 years."  (Source:  History of Stoke Park - see http://www.stokepark.com/book/chapter4.pdf)
