1 NOTE In English John VI. John became prince of Brazil in 1788. In 1792, after 
2 CONT Maria became insane, John ruled in her name; in 1799 he formally became 
2 CONT regent. During the Napoleonic Wars, in 1801 and 1807, the French invaded 
2 CONT Portugal. John fled to Brazil and made it the center of his government. 
2 CONT Brazil was declared a separate kingdom in 1815, and when Maria died, John 
2 CONT succeeded her. While he was in Brazil, a democratic constitution was 
2 CONT adopted in Portugal. John swore to abide by the new constitution and 
2 CONT appointed his son Pedro as regent. John returned to Portugal in 1821. In 
2 CONT 1824 John suppressed a revolt against the liberals, which was led by his 
2 CONT wife and his younger son, Dom Miguel.
