2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1820-1832/member/finch-george-1794-1870#biography]
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the Earl of Winchilsea's death, the house at Burley-on-the-Hill and the estates in Rutland, Buckinghamshire and Essex passed to his illegitimate son, George Finch - son of Mrs. Phoebe Thompson.  They also had a daughter Georg
2 CONC iana Augustus Finch who married John Drummond.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earl of Winchilsea's mother refused to let him marry Phoebe as she thought he could do better, however he often took Georgiana and George, who lived with their mother in London, to his home in Burley on the Hill. 
