1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Penn''' (22 February 1760 - 21 June 1834) was an English politician and writer who was the chief proprietor of the Province of Pennsylvania from 1775 to 1776. He and his cousin, John Penn ("John Penn, the G
2 CONC overnor") held unsold property, of 24,000,000 acres (97,000 km2), which the Pennsylvania legislature confiscated after the American Revolution. ''(Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0)''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
