1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===18 May 1768===
2 CONT Baptism of Caroline Conyers in Epping, Essex  (Source:  FHL microfilm 571180)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Caroline was the youngest daughter of John Conyers Esq. and of the Lady Harriet* Conyers his wife" (Inscription on monument at Clare Church)  
2 CONT
2 CONT *other sources list her name to be Henrietta, not Harriet.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1799, April 10===
2 CONT '''Caroline Conyers''' was married by the Reverend Edward Conyers (Vicar of Epping, Essex) in her Parish of St. George's, Hanover Square to '''John Barker, Esq., of Chatham Barracks''', Kent,.  Witnesses were John Conyers and Augu
2 CONC sta Sophia Feilding. (Source:  Register book of marriages belonging to the parish, Vol.2)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1804===
2 CONT Her husband Colonel John Barker died (he was the son of John Barker (the younger brother to Martha), and bequeathed "Clare Priory" to his widow, Caroline  (source "List of the Owners of Clare Priory") - following this her daughter
2 CONC  Caroline Baker (nee Barker) lived at Clare Priory (see next paragraph).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1832 Report of the Society for the Propagation of the Gospel in Foreign Parts:
2 CONT Castle Hedingham Deanery Committee (est. 1822)===
2 CONT :  the following were all related:
2 CONT * '''1827 Barnardiston, Nathaniel, Esq., Ryes Lodge, Little Henney'''
2 CONT * '''1828 Barker, Mrs., Clare Priory, Clare, Suffolk'''
2 CONT * '''1828 Conyers, Mrs., Clare Priory, Clare, Suffolk'''
2 CONT * '''1828 Greenwood, Charles, Esq., Auberies, near Sudbury'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1841 Census===
2 CONT Caroline (Conyers) Barker's daughter Caroline Barker married George Baker, and Caroline (Conyers)  '''age 70''' (therefore b. c.1871) and the Baker family are recorded in the '''1841 Census as living at Clare Priory''':
2 CONT * '''Caroline Barker	70'''
2 CONT * George Baker	45
2 CONT * Caroline Baker	35 (daughter of Caroline Barker, aged 70)
2 CONT * Charlotte Baker	12
2 CONT * George Baker	11
2 CONT * William Baker	10
2 CONT * Edward Baker	4
2 CONT * John Baker	2
2 CONT * N K 	3 Mo
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1848===
2 CONT
2 CONT  '''January 8, 1848.'''  
2 CONT Visitors to '''Clare Church - St. Peter and St. Paul  chapel''' can view two hatchments dedicated to Caroline and her husband John Barker. "Devoted to her maternal duties, and to the exemplary discharge of every other Christian re
2 CONC lation.  She survived her beloved Husband during a period of 43 years.  Passed at Clare Priory;  Where, esteemed and respected by all, and deeply lamented by her poorer neighbours, 
2 CONT ===She entered into her rest.  January 8th 1848, In the 80th Year of her Age.===
2 CONT
2 CONT England & Wales, FreeBMD Death Index: 1837-1915 about Caroline Barker
