1 NOTE Eight-year-old Louis XVII was recognized as king by French Royalists after 
2 CONT his father's execution during the French Revolution. According to official 
2 CONT reports, he died of tuberculosis while a prisoner of the Republican 
2 CONT government in Paris. Many believed that he had escaped, however, and more 
2 CONT than 30 people later claimed to be the "Lost Dauphin."
1 NOTE Louis Charles XVII was the son of Louis XVI, who died on the guillotine in 1793.  Young 8-year old Louis XVII became the next King of France.  His short reign to 1795 was spent in prison, where he died at age 10 in 1795.  Last of 
2 CONC the house of Bourbon Dynasty which began in 1589 with Henry IV.
