2 CONT Diese Seite wurde zuletzt am 8. April 2010 um 04:02 Uhr geändert.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Archduchess Maria Leopoldina Josepha Caroline of Austria; (22 January 1797 – 11 December 1826), Empress consort of Pedro I of Brazil, and, for two months, simultaneously Queen consort of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Vienna, Austria, the daughter of Francis II, Holy Roman Emperor, and his second wife, Maria Teresa of the Two Sicilies. Among her many siblings were Emperor Ferdinand I of Austria and Archduchess Marie Louise, the 
2 CONC wife of Napoleon Bonaparte.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1817 she sailed to Brazil to marry the future crown prince of Portugal, Dom Pedro of Alcântara. The Portuguese royal family had been living there in exile for ten years, as a result of the Napoleonic Wars. Leopoldine was highly
2 CONC  cultured, fluent in six languages, and very interested in the natural sciences. In the years that followed she brought several researchers and biologists to her new homeland, starting with Johann Baptist von Spix, Carl Friedrich 
2 CONC Philipp von Martius, and Johann Natterer, who accompanied her in 1817.
2 CONT
2 CONT When his father, King João VI, returned to Lisbon in 1821, Dom Pedro chose to remain in Brazil with Leopoldine and their children. In 1822, Dom Pedro headed Brazil's declaration of independence from Portugal, and was crowned as th
2 CONC e country's Emperor. Princess Leopoldina thus became Brazil's first Empress consort. She also played an important role on the Declaration of Independence process. The princess found out that Portugal was preparing an action agains
2 CONC t Brazil and, having no time to wait for D. Pedro's return, Leopoldina, advised by José Bonifácio, and using its interim power, met on September 2, 1822 with the State of Council, signed the Independence decree, declaring Brazil s
2 CONC eparated from Portugal. The Empress sent her husband a letter demanding him to announce the Independência do Brasil and warned him, "The fruit is ready, it's time to harvest."
2 CONT
2 CONT When his father died, on 10 March 1826, Pedro inherited the Portuguese throne as King Pedro IV, while remaining Emperor Pedro I of Brazil. However, only two months later, he was forced to give up the Portuguese throne to his seven
2 CONC -year-old daughter Maria, But for a couple of months, Leopoldine was both Empress consort in Brazil and Queen consort in Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leopoldine and Pedro had seven children before she died in 1826 following a miscarriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
