1 NOTE To escape a French invasion of Portugal, Pedro and his parents fled to 
2 CONT Brazil in 1807. In 1821, when his father returned home, Pedro became 
2 CONT prince regent of Brazil. The following year he proclaimed Brazilian 
2 CONT independence and was crowned emperor of Brazil. Proclaimed king of 
2 CONT Portugal in 1826, he abdicated that same year in favor of his daughter 
2 CONT Maria II (1819-53). Pedro's arbitrary rule and his involvement in the 
2 CONT internal affairs of Portugal caused his popularity to wane in Brazil. He 
2 CONT abdicated as emperor of Brazil in 1831 and returned to Portugal, where he 
2 CONT supported Maria against his brother Dom Miguel, her rival for the throne.
