1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "George Berkeley (British Army officer)
2 CONT General Sir George Henry Frederick Berkeley KCB (9 July 1785 – 25 September 1857) was a British Army officer and Conservative politician.
2 CONT Sir George Berkeley
2 CONT Born
2 CONT 9 July 1785
2 CONT Died
2 CONT 25 September 1857 (aged 72)
2 CONT Allegiance
2 CONT -Rank
2 CONT General
2 CONT -Commands held
2 CONT Madras Army
2 CONT Battles/wars
2 CONT Waterloo Campaign
2 CONT Crimean War
2 CONT -Awards
2 CONT Knight Commander of the Order of the Bath
2 CONT
2 CONT -Military career
2 CONT Berkeley was the eldest son of Admiral Sir George Cranfield Berkeley, third son of Augustus Berkeley, 4th Earl of Berkeley. His mother was Lady Emilia Charlotte, daughter of Lord George Lennox.
2 CONT At the start of the Waterloo Campaign of 1815, he was the Duke of Wellington's liaison officer at the Prince of Orange's headquarters. He was also created KCB in 1815. He became Commander-in-Chief of the Madras Army in 1848 and Su
2 CONC rveyor-General of the Ordnance in 1852.
2 CONT He was given the colonelcy of the 81st Regiment of Foot in 1844, transferring in 1845 to the 35th Regiment of Foot, a position he held until his death. He was promoted full general on 20 June 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Political career
2 CONT Berkeley was returned to Parliament for Devonport in 1852, a seat he held until 1857.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Family
2 CONT Berkeley died in September 1857, aged 72.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had married Lucy, daughter of Sir Thomas Sutton, 1st Baronet, in 1815. They had three sons and one daughter. His third son, George, succeeded as 7th Earl of Berkeley in 1882. Lady Berkeley died in February 1870."
2 CONT [https://www.wikiwand.com/en/George_Berkeley_(British_Army_officer)?fbclid=IwAR2XENUYOoS3PbUC6K1tCMnOjgqZ7-T9s9uADrGoJ-D9Cotb3A4Z_Pgr9Mw]
