1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugo Shelley Light (1834-1893) Capt. 68th (Durham). Born at Genova in Italy on 11 May 1834. His parents were Hugh Aldborough Bowen and Mary Light (née Bennet). Hugo enlisted with the 68th (Durham) Regiment of Foot 
2 CONC (Light Infantry) ('The Faithful Durhams') in 1853. He served in the Crimea and during the New Zealand Wars. Hugo took part in the Battle of Gate Pā | Pukehinahina in Tauranga on 29 April 1864. He and Margaret Lucy Bailey married a
2 CONC t Florence in Italy in 1886. Hugo died at South Kensington in London on 8 August 1893. He was buried in Brompton Cemetery. Aged 59. Bio by Debbie McCauley (2025) via https://debbiemccauleyauthor.wordpress.com/heritage/cultural-her
