1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Illegitimate son of the Earl of Winchilsea and heir to the house at Burley-on-the-Hill and the estates in Rutland, Buckinghamshire and Essex (His mother was Mrs. Phoebe Thompson).  
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his sister who lived with their mother in Brompton, London, often visited their father at Burley on the Hill.
2 CONT
2 CONT George entered Harrow in 1805 under the name of Thompson, but subsequently took that of Finch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Entered Cambridge (but left without a degree.)  Later admitted to the Middle Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source:  FINCH, George (1794-1870), of Burley-on-the-Hill, nr. Oakham, Rutland;  Published in The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1820-1832, ed. D.R. Fisher, 2009;  Cambridge University Press]
