2 CONT 1847 Death of Henrietta Juliana Jenkinson, nee Baker
2 CONT
2 CONT ===A letter from G. Baker (George) to (his wife's nephew) Captain (later Admiral) George Hills attests to the death of Harriet as follows:===
2 CONT '''Clare Priory, April 21st ''(no year given)'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT "My Dear Captain.
2 CONT
2 CONT  It is with much pain that I have to communicate the death of my poor dear Sister Harriet**Jenkinson who as I find by a Letter from Norbiton this morning was taken from us on Monday ,,,,, ***The state of her health for some time p
2 CONC ast had been such as to cause us great anxiety and during the whole of last week there appears to have been little hope of her rallying. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert ***Jenkinson particularly requests me to make known this event to you, but the state of his own health and nerves is such as not only to make writing an irksome effort, but it would even be painful to him to receive letters
2 CONC  on the subject. I collect this from my Mother's report, and therefore do not write to him myself, and it would I think be kind in you to abstain from doing so. 
2 CONT
2 CONT With our joint kind regards, Believe me, Very truly yours, GBaker "(signature)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrietta's Death is registered as per: [Event Place:	 Kingston, Surrey, England
2 CONT * Volume:	 4
2 CONT * Page:	 159
2 CONT * Line Number:	 119]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Henrietta Juliana.  Harriet is a spoken form of Henrietta.
2 CONT
2 CONT **This would have been '''Monday April 19th 1847'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *** Harriet's husband Robert Henry Jenkinson 1786-1857.
