1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Will of Thomas Mustain, 1791 - Pittsylvania Co. VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Thomas Mustain weak in body. Dead Book 9, pg 119-120, written 6 November 1791, probated 16 July 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT To my beloved wife Mary Mustain, a sufficient maintenance suitable to her  surcomstance, free and undesturbed during her life or widowhood.
2 CONT
2 CONT To my son Jesse, 200 acres to be taken off the upper end of the tract where  I now live. The rest of this tract to be sold.
2 CONT
2 CONT To daughter, Rebeckah and Molly, twenty shillings each from the sale of the  above land. To daughters Mary Ann and Sally, ten pounds each.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Avery Mustain and Daughters Anna Buckner, Milley Keese, Tabeth a Bruce, Winney Lewis and Siludey Shelton one equal part of the money from the
2 CONT
2 CONT sale of the land.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Thomas Mustain, son of Jesse Mustain and his wife Jenney, has promised to  live with me and my wife during our lives for which I give and bequeath unto the said Thomas Mustain a tract of land on both sides of Nixes Creek, 170  
2 CONC acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT The balance of my moveable property to be divided among my last six named  children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Appoint son Jesse Mustain and Joel Shelton executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thoams (X) Mustain Witnesses:  Francis (X) Ivy, Nathaniel Faris, Griffith Dickinson, Vincent
2 CONT
2 CONT Shelton and Charles Lewis, Jr.  security for executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Submitter note:  In the Will of Thomas Mustain when he said " My son Avery Mustain and daughters..." the daughters he lists are Thomas's daughters, NOT Avery's.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Submitted by E. S. Rick McDaniel <chefrick@ioa.com>
