1 NOTE He succeeded to the throne at the age of five, on his father's abdication, 
2 CONT and was subject to a regency until he reached his majority in 1840. The 
2 CONT early years of his reign were marked by revolts in various parts of the 
2 CONT country. Pedro had a lifelong interest in science and was a patron of the 
2 CONT arts. He opposed slavery, which he gradually phased out of Brazilian life 
2 CONT -- outlawing the slave trade in 1850, initiating a process of emancipation 
2 CONT in 1871, and finally abolishing slavery altogether in 1888. Under his rule 
2 CONT Brazil fought a costly but successful war with Paraguay (1864-70), gaining 
2 CONT some territory as a result. Although impartial toward Brazil's rival 
2 CONT political groups, Pedro's use of the wide powers given to him by the 
2 CONT imperial constitution caused resentment, which, along with dissatisfaction 
2 CONT among slave owners, led to his overthrow and the establishment of a 
2 CONT republic in 1889.
