2 CONT
2 CONT      Friedrich Maria Erzherzog von Österreich was born on 4 June 1856 at Gross-Seelowitz, Morav. ▼2, ▼3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Karl Ferdinand Erzherzog von Österreich and Elizabeth Franziska Maria Erzherzogin von Österreich. ▼1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabelle Hedwig Franziska Natalie Prinzessin von Croÿ, daughter of Rudolf Maximilian Konstantin Herzog von Croÿ and Natalie de Ligne, Princesse de Ligne, on 8 October 1878 at Château de l'Hermitage, Belgium. ▼2, ▼3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 30 December 1936 at age 80 at Ungarisch-Altenburg, Hungary. ▼2
2 CONT
2 CONT      Friedrich Maria Erzherzog von Österreich was a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine. He gained the title of Erzherzog von Österreich (styled as HI&RH Archduke of Austria). ▼1 He was baptised with the name of Friedrich Mar
2 CONC ia Albrecht Wilhelm Karl. ▼1 He gained the rank of General Field Marshal in the service of the Prussian Army. ▼3 He gained the rank of Field Marshal in the service of the Austrian Army. ▼3 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Herzog v
2 CONC on Teschen on 18 February 1895. ▼4, ▼3
2 CONT
