2 CONT Friedrich Maria Erzherzog von Österreich was born on 4 June 1856 at Gross-Seelowitz, Morav.2,3 He was the son of Karl Ferdinand Erzherzog von Österreich and Elizabeth Franziska Maria Erzherzogin von Österreich.1 He married Isabell
2 CONC e Hedwig Franziska Natalie Prinzessin von Croÿ, daughter of Rudolf Maximilian Konstantin Herzog von Croÿ and Natalie de Ligne, Princesse de Ligne, on 8 October 1878 at Château de l'Hermitage, Condé-sur-l'Escaut, France.2,3 He died
2 CONC  on 30 December 1936 at age 80 at Ungarisch-Altenburg, Hungary.2
2 CONT      He was a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine. He gained the title of Erzherzog von Österreich (styled as HI&RH Archduke of Austria).1 He was given the name of Friedrich Maria Albrecht Wilhelm Karl at birth.1 He gained th
2 CONC e rank of Field Marshal in the service of the Austrian Army.3 He gained the rank of General Field Marshal in the service of the Prussian Army.3 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Herzog von Teschen on 18 February 1895.4,3
