1 NOTE Amadeus or Amadeo of Turin, Duke of Aosta, was elected King of Spain by the Spanish Cortes after their unsuccessful attempt to persuade prince of Hohenzollern (Leopold) to accept the crown following the revolution of 1868 in which
2 CONC  Queen Isabella was deposed. Amadeus/Amadeo atempted to exercise authority, but was disliked and abdicated in 1873. following the outbreak of the Carlist civil war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus, of the House of Savoy, ruled Spain from 1870, but was deposed in 1873, and was succeeded by the House of Bourbon.
1 NOTE DUKE OF AOSTA; HAD 1 SON, PRINCE HUMBERT (1889-1918)
