1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=78550954&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT Veteran of the American Civil War. Served in Co. F, 4th Louisiana Infantry, CSA. Rank: Lieutenant <nowiki>-------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Victorin Duralde: father of Irene Victoria Edwards (née Duralde). Margaret Smith: mother of Irene Victoria Edwards (née Duralde).
2 CONT
2 CONT *Source: Cook County, IL death certificate, issued in 1927 for Irene Victoria Edwards
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph "Victor" Duralde later married Emily Bynum. No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Victor, at age 40, along with his wife, Emily Bynum Duralde, age 34, died of yellow fever, during a three month epidemic that took the lives of 236 persons, in and around Baton Rouge (Weekly Advocate, Baton Rouge, 29 Nov 18
2 CONC 78, pg. 3).
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary: --In Baton Rouge. on Monday, October 7th, 1878, at his residence on Union [St.,] of yellow fever, JOSEPH VICTOR DURALDE, Jr., a native and ex-Sheriff of West Baton Rouge Parish, aged 40 years.
2 CONT
