0 @N6000000002322305556@ NOTE Seems that there were two Holy Roman Emperors during this period, with
1 CONT Charles being elected in opposition to the Habsburg Maria Theresa's husband,
1 CONT Francis, grand duke of Tuscany. Also, there were antipopes and ever changing
1 CONT true popes who may not have known who was in charge of the many different
1 CONT kingdoms. As well, there were "claimants" who would simply name themselves to
1 CONT different thrones. Charles's claim was due to his marriage to the daughter of
1 CONT the Emperor. Charles was crowned as Bavaria was being overrun by Austria.
