0 @N6000000002176689923@ NOTE He was duc d' Montpensier from 1747, duc d' Chartres from 1752 and duc d'
1 CONT Orleans from 1785. His liberal ways found him temporarily banished from the
1 CONT court for challenging the king's authority (1787) before the Parlement of
1 CONT Paris. Aiding in the French Revolution against the crown, he renounced his
1 CONT title and accepted the name of Philippe Egalite on the fall of the monarachy
1 CONT in 1792. Accused of being an accomplice of Dumouriez, he was arrested and
1 CONT guillotined in 1793. His son would become the final monarch of France.
