0 @N6000000002322348297@ NOTE His reign was disastrous to Spain, which lost all American colonies, as well
1 CONT as European power. His cruel, repressive policies provoked many rebellions.
1 CONT Becoming King upon forced abdication of his father in 1808, Ferdinand was
1 CONT imprisoned by Napoleon 1808-14 and forced to relinquish his crown (France run
1 CONT by Joseph Bonaparte 1808-1813), but his crown was restored after Napoleon's
1 CONT fall in 1814. Tyrannical, absolute rule continued, and after his death came
1 CONT the war between supporters of daughter Isabella and brother Don Carlos.
