0 @N6000000002176664296@ NOTE Historic evidence here his badly lacking. Encyclopaedia Britannica states
1 CONT that "George" succeeded his brother Albert, but there is no other mention
1 CONT anywhere about this "George". What is known about this time is that a Saxony
1 CONT king, two days before the Germans surrendered at the end of World War I in
1 CONT 1918, was forced to abdicate. Was this Saxony king "George"? Then, a republic
1 CONT was proclaimed and Saxony became a part of one of the founding states of the
1 CONT German Republic. After Germany's defeat in W War II, Saxony was liquidated.
