0 @N6000000002176664276@ NOTE An artillery officer at age 15, Albert later commanded the German army of
1 CONT occupation in France. Soon after, he was made inspector general of the
1 CONT imperial German Army and was promoted to the rank of field marshal. As king
1 CONT of Saxony, Albert was mainly interested in military affairs but approved
1 CONT reforms in local administration, education, and taxation and encouraged
1 CONT industrialization. He left no children and was succeeded by his brother
1 CONT George.
