0 @N6000000002322348573@ NOTE Son of Charles Albert, he became the first king of a united Italy. Though
1 CONT there were problems between the two of them, Pope Pius IX and Victor, the
1 CONT Pope allowed Victor to be burried in the Pantheon. He was awarded the crown
1 CONT over a united Italy upon the disposition of Francis II, King of Two Sicilies.
1 CONT He had been the king of Sardinia-Piedmot (northern Italy) and with Naples and
1 CONT Sicily, he acquired southern Italy. Succession went to Umberto I, #1576.
1 CONT See the last of the Bourbons, King Francis II, #1575.
