0 @N6000000002322315581@ NOTE A man whose naive liberalism proved unequal to the international intrigues
1 CONT that had put him on the throne as Emperor of Mexico, and the brutal struggles
1 CONT within Mexico that led to his execution on a hill outside Queretaro. Crowned
1 CONT emperor on June 10, 1864, Maximilian intended to rule with paternal
1 CONT benevolence, viewing himself as a protector of the Indian peasants, but the
1 CONT withdrawal in 1867 of French forces in Mexico supporting the small army of
1 CONT Maximilian enabled Juarez's army to surround, starve and defeat his.
